\pard\ql\li0\ri0\fi0\sb0\sa80\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs40\b\cf1 RiqatonyPad Documentation}\par
\pard\ql\li0\ri0\fi0\sb0\sa240\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs26\i A lightweight Rich Text Format (RTF) editor.}\par
\pard\ql\li0\ri0\fi0\sb100\sa100\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs30\b\cf1 Welcome}\par
\pard\ql\li0\ri0\fi0\sb0\sa120\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs24 RiqatonyPad is dedicated to .rtf documents. It provides rich-text editing, file-safety controls, printing and PDF export while keeping RTF interoperability as the persistence target. RiqatonyPad is not a DOCX or PDF editor.}\par
\pard\ql\li0\ri0\fi0\sb100\sa100\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs30\b\cf1 Getting started}\par
\pard\ql\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa60\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs24 \u8226?\tab Create a new RTF document with File > New, or open another independent editor window with File > New Window.}\par
\pard\ql\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa60\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs24 \u8226?\tab Open an existing .rtf file with File > Open.}\par
\pard\ql\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa60\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs24 \u8226?\tab Use Save or Save As to write Rich Text Format. RiqatonyPad saves .rtf documents only.}\par
\pard\ql\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa60\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs24 \u8226?\tab Use File > More Actions for Duplicate File, Rename File, Delete File, Open in External Editor, Open Containing Folder and Properties.}\par
\pard\ql\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa60\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs24 \u8226?\tab Use Locked Mode when you want to inspect a document without editing it. F12 toggles Locked Mode.}\par
\pard\ql\li0\ri0\fi0\sb100\sa100\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs30\b\cf1 File safety and external changes}\par
\pard\ql\li0\ri0\fi0\sb0\sa120\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs24 RiqatonyPad watches an opened file for changes made outside the application. If the file changes on disk, the editor can show an external-change banner with Reload from Disk and Save Version As options. Save operations also check for external changes before replacing the file.}\par
\pard\ql\li0\ri0\fi0\sb0\sa120\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs24 If the original backing file disappears while the document is open, RiqatonyPad keeps the live document in memory and offers Save Version As, Recreate Original, Close Without Saving or Cancel before that live copy can be discarded.}\par
\pard\ql\li0\ri0\fi0\sb0\sa120\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs24 Settings also provides policies for Duplicate File with Unsaved Changes and Open Externally with Unsaved Changes. These can be left on Ask Every Time or changed to the alternatives shown in the Settings menu.}\par
\pard\ql\li0\ri0\fi0\sb100\sa100\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs30\b\cf1 Formatting}\par
\pard\ql\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa60\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs24 \u8226?\tab Font family and size, bold, italic, underline, strikethrough, superscript and subscript.}\par
\pard\ql\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa60\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs24 \u8226?\tab Text colour and highlighting.}\par
\pard\ql\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa60\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs24 \u8226?\tab Normal Paragraph and Heading 1 through Heading 6 paragraph styles.}\par
\pard\ql\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa60\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs24 \u8226?\tab Left, Centre, Right and Justify alignment.}\par
\pard\ql\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa60\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs24 \u8226?\tab Indent and Outdent, paragraph spacing and line spacing at 1.0, 1.15, 1.5 and 2.0.}\par
\pard\ql\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa60\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs24 \u8226?\tab Bulleted lists and Clear Formatting.}\par
\pard\ql\li0\ri0\fi0\sb100\sa100\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs30\b\cf1 Insert and tables}\par
\pard\ql\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa60\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs24 \u8226?\tab Insert PNG/JPEG images and hyperlinks. Existing links can be edited or removed.}\par
\pard\ql\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa60\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs24 \u8226?\tab Insert simple non-nested tables and use Table Editing to add or remove rows and columns, or delete the table.}\par
\pard\ql\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa60\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs24 \u8226?\tab Insert Date and Time, Date Only or Time Only.}\par
\pard\ql\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa60\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs24 \u8226?\tab Insert horizontal rules and symbols.}\par
\pard\ql\li0\ri0\fi0\sb100\sa100\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs30\b\cf1 Find and navigation}\par
\pard\ql\li0\ri0\fi0\sb0\sa120\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs24 Edit > Find opens the Find panel; Find and Replace opens the replacement controls. F3 moves to the next match, Shift+F3 moves to the previous match, and Esc closes the Find/Replace panel when it is visible.}\par
\pard\ql\li0\ri0\fi0\sb100\sa100\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs30\b\cf1 New document defaults}\par
\pard\ql\li0\ri0\fi0\sb0\sa120\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs24 Brand-new documents use the saved font family, size, style, line spacing and alignment. The factory baseline is Sans Serif, 12 pt, Normal, 1.15 line spacing and Left. View > Editor Miscellaneous > New Document Defaults changes future new documents without reformatting the open file.}\par
\pard\ql\li0\ri0\fi0\sb100\sa100\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs30\b\cf1 Ribbon, Retro and AppMenu-only}\par
\pard\ql\li0\ri0\fi0\sb0\sa120\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs24 Ribbon is the default interface. Ribbon and Retro use the same shared command registry and command actions. Icon-only toolbar buttons expose command names and shortcuts in their tooltips.}\par
\pard\ql\li0\ri0\fi0\sb0\sa120\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs24 View > Editor Toolbar offers Ribbon (default), Retro, Retro Settings, and Disabled (AppMenu only). Ctrl+Alt+Shift+T toggles directly between Ribbon and Retro; Disabled (AppMenu only) is chosen from the menu when you want neither toolbar visible.}\par
\pard\ql\li0\ri0\fi0\sb0\sa120\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs24 Retro uses one horizontally scrollable 52 px row. Use the mouse wheel or one-finger drag when the row overflows; there is no toolbar overflow arrow. Retro Settings selects the optional commands and selectors shown on Retro. Clear All removes all optional controls, Default restores the standard set, and the Retro Settings control itself always remains at the end of the Retro row so the toolbar can be configured again.}\par
\pard\ql\li0\ri0\fi0\sb0\sa120\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs24 Right-click the Ribbon or Retro surface to switch toolbar mode or open Retro Settings. In Ribbon, Ctrl+Tab and Ctrl+Shift+Tab move between ribbon tabs. Double-click a ribbon tab title to collapse the controls; click a tab title once to reveal them again.}\par
\pard\ql\li0\ri0\fi0\sb100\sa100\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs30\b\cf1 View and editor layout}\par
\pard\ql\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa60\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs24 \u8226?\tab Full Screen (F11) toggles the main window full-screen state.}\par
\pard\ql\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa60\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs24 \u8226?\tab Show Status controls the status bar.}\par
\pard\ql\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa60\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs24 \u8226?\tab Word Wrap controls editor wrapping.}\par
\pard\ql\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa60\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs24 \u8226?\tab Dark Editor changes only the document canvas; it is independent from the application chrome.}\par
\pard\ql\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa60\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs24 \u8226?\tab Locked Mode (F12) disables editing until it is turned off.}\par
\pard\ql\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa60\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs24 \u8226?\tab Editor Layout provides four arrangements: Toolbar Top / Find Bottom, Toolbar Top / Find Top, Toolbar Bottom / Find Top and Toolbar Bottom / Find Bottom.}\par
\pard\ql\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa60\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs24 \u8226?\tab Editor Zoom provides Zoom In, Zoom Out and Reset Zoom.}\par
\pard\ql\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa60\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs24 \u8226?\tab Editor Miscellaneous contains Tab Width and New Document Defaults.}\par
\pard\ql\li0\ri0\fi0\sb100\sa100\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs30\b\cf1 Application themes, icons and settings}\par
\pard\ql\li0\ri0\fi0\sb0\sa120\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs24 Settings > App Theme offers Light, Dark and System for the application chrome. On Windows, System follows the Windows app light/dark preference. On Linux and other platforms System remains native to Qt and the desktop environment. Dark Editor remains a separate canvas setting.}\par
\pard\ql\li0\ri0\fi0\sb0\sa120\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs24 Settings > App Icons defines four Riqa icon families: Harmony, Humility, Heritage and Halcyon. The packaged Windows and AppImage builds include all four families.}\par
\pard\ql\li0\ri0\fi0\sb0\sa120\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs24 Settings > App Drag-and-Drop chooses whether a dropped document opens on the active window or in a new window. The Settings menu also contains the unsaved-change policies used by Duplicate File and Open in External Editor.}\par
\pard\ql\li0\ri0\fi0\sb100\sa100\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs30\b\cf1 Keyboard Shortcuts}\par
\pard\ql\li0\ri0\fi0\sb0\sa120\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs24 Help > Keyboard Shortcuts shows the live QAction shortcut inventory used by the running application. Search matches command names and shortcut tokens, including modifier aliases; the Menu filter narrows the list. Treat this dialog as the authoritative complete shortcut reference for the installed build.}\par
\pard\ql\li0\ri0\fi0\sb100\sa100\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs30\b\cf1 Useful shortcuts}\par
\pard\ql\li0\ri0\fi0\sb0\sa100\sl276\slmult1 {\plain\f0\fs24\i This is a compact selection only. Use Help > Keyboard Shortcuts for the complete live list.}\par
